    "q-100137": {
      "dom_id": "step-q100137",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find the value of $3+(-2+7)^{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nWe begin by performing the operations inside the parentheses. So, first we add $(-2)$ to $7$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3+(-2+7)^{2} & =3+{5}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we compute the exponent:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3+{5}^{2} & =3+25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we add the numbers: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3+25=28\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
